# Scenario 'forced_debug' (FORCED execution, published under traces/forced/, never part of the natural union): the three debug screens that no ROM path calls.
# Each segment power-cycles, boots to the logo screen and then jumps into the routine with the harness directive `force BB:AAAA` (docs/research/dynamic_tracing.md,
# section 11: the ROM's own far-call helper 00:06D1 is entered with a stub in WRAM at $CE00; when the routine returns the machine spins in the stub).
#   1. 19:4000 DebugFlags_Run ("== DEBUG MODE ==", one entry 【サインアップデバッグフラグ】 = the byte at SRAM bank 1 $B0BF): DOWN/UP change the entry, LEFT/RIGHT the digit cursor, A
#      changes the digit/bit, START switches BIT/DEC, holding a direction gives the auto-repeat, B/SELECT leave.
#   2. 19:4980 Debug_ErrorScreenTest ("A:エラー B+↑↓:しゅるい Sel:END ↑↓(←→):Number"): a kind (B+UP/DOWN) and a 16-bit number are edited, A opens the ROM's error screen 5C:5150
#      with that kind/number, A closes it (B is held for at least the auto-repeat delay: B+UP then adds 1-2 to the kind).
#   3. 1B:4040 SoundTest_Run ("Ａ：ＭＵＳＩＣ Ｂ：ＳＯＵＮＤ Ｓｔａ：ＳＴＯＰ"): a 16-bit id is edited, A plays it as music, B as a sound effect, START stops, SELECT leaves.
# Starts from the state left by 'tutorial_profile'. Screen names = my reading of the screenshots.
# ---- 1. debug flags
reset
wait 400
waitstable 60 max 600
gap 30
force 19:4000
wait 200
shot flags_start
tap RIGHT
wait 30
tap A
wait 30
shot flags_a
tap RIGHT x3
wait 60
tap A x2
wait 30
tap UP
wait 30
tap DOWN
wait 30
shot flags_edit
tap START
wait 40
shot flags_bit
tap RIGHT x9
wait 30
tap A x3
wait 30
hold RIGHT 120
wait 30
hold UP 120
wait 30
hold A 200
wait 30
shot flags_bit_edit
tap START
wait 40
tap START
wait 40
shot flags_hex
tap B
wait 200
shot flags_exit
